# Dependencies
node_modules/

# State + secrets
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.env
.env.local
.mini-ork/runs/
.mini-ork/INBOX/
.mini-ork/locks/
.mini-ork/secrets/
.mini-ork/state/
.mini-ork/worktrees/
# v0.2-pt16 (SAFETY): cl_*.sh wrappers source secrets.local.sh per-dispatch
# (see lib/providers/cl_glm.sh comment block). The documented path is
# ${MINI_ORK_HOME}/config/secrets.local.sh — must be ignored everywhere
# it can appear. Defense-in-depth: also ignore any *secrets.local* shape.
.mini-ork/config/secrets.local.sh
**/secrets.local.sh
**/secrets.local.*
*.local.secrets
# Per-developer local env preferences (non-secret). Same gitignored
# pattern as secrets.local.sh; holds prefs like MO_REVIEW_LLM_LENSES=1
# that an individual machine wants on by default. Sourced from
# .githooks/pre-push right after MINI_ORK_HOME is established.
.mini-ork/config/local.sh
**/.mini-ork/config/local.sh
# Local provider registry may name private endpoints/models — never commit.
# (It SHADOWS config/providers.yaml entirely: first-hit resolution, no merge.)
.mini-ork/config/providers.yaml

# Per-developer Claude Code workspace — never ship to OSS.
# Covers session memory, handoffs, scheduled task state, settings overrides.
.claude/

# Local kickoffs are user-authored, session-specific, and may name internal
# projects or customers. Keep them out of the OSS tree.
.mini-ork/kickoffs/

# Local build / cache artifacts
.pnpm-store/
.runtime/
mini_ork/web/static/
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Commercial / private deliverables (e.g. customer-specific business plans).
# Open-source repo carries the recipe, not the customer-named output.
docs/business-plans/

# Runtime locks
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Build artifacts
dist/
design/

# Temp + logs
/tmp/
*.log
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
# verify step writes verifier-result-*.json to cwd on direct runs
/verifier-result-*.json
# framework-edit implementer writes implementer_summary.json to cwd on direct runs
/implementer_summary.json

# Unrelated local scratch projects that share this working tree but are not
# part of mini-ork. Keep them out of the OSS repo.
/peltier-thermal/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor / tooling
.claude/settings.local.json

.mini-ork/state.db
.mini-ork/state.db.*
docs/blog/

# Local research notes/instructions that are useful on this machine but should
# not ship as project documentation.
docs/research/local/

# External-IP guard: these artifact classes carry private external-project
# IP and must never enter this public repo.
Volumes/
.mo-run-home/
/doc-part_*.md
/lens-minimax.md
# Whole research-notes dir holds local arxiv/conductor scaffolding (incl. PDFs),
# not shippable project docs.
.mini-ork/research-notes/
kickoffs/*autonomy-pluggability*

# internal-docs/ is internal-only R&D (arxiv-driven research, architecture
# design notes, runbooks, impl-analysis of other projects) — not shippable OSS
# docs. Keep it on disk locally; never track it in this public repo.
internal-docs/

# Local dev-tooling artifacts (machine-specific, not project deliverables):
# CodeGraph index/config, MCP server wiring, per-machine provider env script.
.codegraph/
codegraph.json
.mcp.json
claude_code_zai_env.sh
*_zai_env.sh

# mini-ork generated state (the engine pointer below is committed)

.mini-ork/*

!.mini-ork/engine
